# Environments
.venv/
.venv-dev/
.pixi/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/

# Deployment secrets and per-machine config
.env

# Per-request working directories (web app)
web_scratch/
# The runs library: whatever a visitor chose to keep, which is their data and
# not this repository's.
web_runs/

# Generated README artefacts (produced by marcs-vibe-coding readme_forge.py)
README.polished.md
README.html
README.preview.html
elementor-widget-markdown.css

# Simulation output -- these are large and regenerable.
# The negations keep the small checked-in example outputs tracked, so the
# analysis tab always has something real to render in tests.
*.fxa
*.xtc
*.dcd
*.chk
flexappeal_output/
*.command
# These negations must match the directory's real case. This Mac's filesystem
# is case-insensitive and the droplet's is not, so a rule with the wrong case
# appears to work locally and matches nothing in production -- the example
# results file would simply be absent there and the Example tab would show its
# "not built yet" page on the live site only. tests/test_deploy.py checks both
# the case on disk and that git does not ignore what the page needs.
!examples/*/*.fxa
!examples/*/output/*.fxa
!examples/*/*.command

# The extracted bundle and the raw capture are both regenerable from the two
# files above by rebuild.sh, and together they are ten megabytes of trajectory
# and repeated progress frames. The log compresses to 22 KB, so the evidence is
# kept in that form.
examples/*/run/
examples/*/terminal.log
examples/*/analyse.log
!examples/*/terminal.log.gz
!examples/*/analyse.log.gz
# The test fixture is a real .fxa from a real run, and the whole analysis suite
# skips without it. Tracked deliberately despite the rule above.
!tests/fixtures/*.fxa

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Exported session transcripts. `/export` drops these in the working directory
# with a dated name, and they are conversation logs rather than source -- they
# have been swept into a commit before by a broad `git add`.
[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-*.txt

# The vendored BoltzMaker clone. Pinned by SHA in vendor/BOLTZMAKER_SHA.txt and
# re-cloned rather than tracked: it is 261 MB of somebody else's history, and a
# copy inside this repository would be a fork nobody meant to make.
vendor/boltzmaker/

# Reference-state build data: downloaded structures, trajectories and the
# analytical store. Large, regenerable, and not this repository's to carry.
data/refs/
data/md/
data/dssp/
data/manifests/

# Reference-state build artefacts: all fetched or derived from public services
# at run time by tools/build_*.py, so they regenerate rather than belonging in
# the history. The cache in particular is keyed on request hashes and would
# grow without limit.
data/cache/
data/md/
data/systems/
data/manifests/

# Private DeepFlex working documents. This repository is public and DeepFlex is
# not, because it discusses an unpublished compound series. These were untracked
# and a single `git add -A` away from being published, which nearly happened
# once in this build; named here so it cannot.
DEEPFLEX_*.md
FXA2_BUILD_PROMPT.md
